# Three.js Scene Graph Structure

## Overview
Three.js uses a hierarchical scene graph where objects can contain other objects. Understanding this structure is essential for parsing and extracting 3D objects.

## Core Classes

### THREE.Object3D
The base class for most objects. Key properties:
- `name` - String identifier for the object
- `children` - Array of child Object3D instances
- `position` - THREE.Vector3 for local position
- `rotation` - THREE.Euler for local rotation
- `quaternion` - THREE.Quaternion for orientation
- `scale` - THREE.Vector3 for local scale
- `matrix` - Local transformation matrix
- `matrixWorld` - World transformation matrix

### THREE.Group
A container object (extends Object3D) used to organize meshes into logical parts:
```javascript
const group = new THREE.Group();
group.name = 'my_part';
group.add(mesh1, mesh2, mesh3);
```

### THREE.Mesh
A renderable 3D object consisting of geometry and material:
```javascript
const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);
mesh.name = 'my_mesh';
```

## Traversing the Scene Graph

### Using traverse()
```javascript
scene.traverse((object) => {
    if (object.isMesh) {
        console.log('Mesh:', object.name);
    }
    if (object.isGroup) {
        console.log('Group:', object.name);
    }
});
```

### Using traverseVisible()
Only traverses visible objects.

### Manual Recursion
```javascript
function walkScene(object, depth = 0) {
    console.log('  '.repeat(depth) + object.name);
    for (const child of object.children) {
        walkScene(child, depth + 1);
    }
}
```

## Getting World Transforms

When exporting meshes, you need world-space coordinates:
```javascript
mesh.updateMatrixWorld(true);
const worldMatrix = mesh.matrixWorld.clone();

// Apply to geometry
const geometry = mesh.geometry.clone();
geometry.applyMatrix4(worldMatrix);
```

## Common Geometry Types

| Geometry Type | Description |
|--------------|-------------|
| BoxGeometry | Rectangular cuboid |
| CylinderGeometry | Cylinder with caps |
| SphereGeometry | UV sphere |
| TorusGeometry | Donut shape |
| ConeGeometry | Cone with base |
| PlaneGeometry | Flat rectangle |

## Finding Parts and Meshes

```javascript
// Find all groups (parts)
const parts = [];
scene.traverse((obj) => {
    if (obj.isGroup && obj.name) {
        parts.push(obj);
    }
});

// Find all meshes in a specific part
const meshesInPart = [];
part.traverse((obj) => {
    if (obj.isMesh) {
        meshesInPart.push(obj);
    }
});
```

## Detecting Object Types

```javascript
object.isMesh       // true for Mesh instances
object.isGroup      // true for Group instances
object.isObject3D   // true for all Object3D instances
object.type         // String like 'Mesh', 'Group', 'Scene'
```

# Converting Three.js Geometry to OBJ Format

## Overview
OBJ is a simple text-based format for 3D geometry. This skill covers converting Three.js BufferGeometry to OBJ format.

## OBJ Format Basics

```
# Comment
o ObjectName
v x y z          # Vertex position
vn x y z         # Vertex normal
vt u v           # Texture coordinate
f v1 v2 v3       # Face (1-indexed vertex indices)
f v1//n1 v2//n2  # Face with normals
```

